  "prompt": "Is the family home deductible from the gross estate, and up to how much?",
  "runtimeCommit": "87ce0c7571f9bd57514b6c2dfb45e9427d19c6b6",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, the family home is deductible from the gross estate, up to a maximum of P10,000,000.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nThe deduction for the family home can significantly impact the estate tax calculation for heirs. By allowing a deduction of up to P10,000,000, it provides a financial relief mechanism for families, ensuring that a substantial portion of the family residence is not subjected to estate tax, thus preserving family assets for the heirs.",
